mod:leave_from_a_silent_trip;
// A `give`, `break L`, `continue L` OR `fall` OUT OF A LOOP CARRIES WHAT EVERY TRIP DID (DEF-546, landing 177d2b2). The loop's
// first walk was silent and dropped the roads it found to outer frames, so a leave on a later trip took the state before the loop:
// `r.value` read an error's zero (60), an unchecked error trapped (74), a page was called sealed (97). Each `*c`/`*n`/`*k` twin is its
// control, refused before and after.
